---
import CaseStudyLayout from '../../components/CaseStudyLayout.astro';
import CaseStudyHero from '../../components/CaseStudyHero.astro';
import CaseStudySection from '../../components/case-study/CaseStudySection.astro';
import CaseStudySubsection from '../../components/case-study/CaseStudySubsection.astro';

const sections = [
	{ id: 'overview', label: 'Overview' },
	{ id: 'research', label: 'Research' },
	{ id: 'ideation', label: 'Ideation' },
	{ id: 'solution', label: 'Solution' },
	{ id: 'reflection', label: 'Reflection' },
];
---

<CaseStudyLayout title="Build IRL — Julia Heo" sections={sections}>
			<!-- TODO: add role, timeframe, and tightened description -->
			<CaseStudyHero
				logo="/images/build-irl/logo.png"
				logoAlt="Build IRL"
				headline="Designing a 0→1 platform for building and running club communities"
				tags={['Product/UX Design', 'Web/Mobile', 'Social']}
				description="A platform for starting, running, and joining clubs in real life — designed to reduce burnout for builders and give joiners a real read on club culture."
			/>

			<CaseStudySection id="overview" title="Overview">
				<CaseStudySubsection title="Context: What is Build IRL?">
					<p>
						Build IRL is a platform for starting and running in-person clubs. It replaces the patchwork of tools
						most builders juggle — messaging, planning, RSVPs — with a single home, and gives joiners a real sense
						of a club's culture before they commit.
					</p>
				</CaseStudySubsection>
				<CaseStudySubsection title="Problem: What issue is Build IRL facing?">
					<p>
						The problem sits on both sides of a club. Builders were burning out on logistics — juggling five-plus
						disconnected tools to run a single club. Joiners were hesitating — they couldn't tell what a club was
						really like without joining first. My job was to figure out which core flows and MVP features would ease
						that friction on both ends.
					</p>
				</CaseStudySubsection>
				<CaseStudySubsection title="Goal: How Might We...">
					<p>
						lower the logistical weight on builders and give joiners a real read on club culture — so both sides can
						commit with confidence?
					</p>
				</CaseStudySubsection>
			</CaseStudySection>

			<CaseStudySection id="research" title="Research">
				<CaseStudySubsection title="Preliminary Audit and Competitive Analysis">
					<p> We audited BuildIRL against its PRD, then benchmarked five adjacent platforms: Partiful, Luma, Meetup, Patreon, and Sweatpals. </p>
					<img src="/images/build-irl/preliminary.png" alt="Preliminary Audit and Analysis" class="research-image" />
					<p> This gave us a baseline for what BuildIRL was, what nearby products were doing, and where to look next. </p>
				</CaseStudySubsection>
				<CaseStudySubsection title="User Interviews with Club Builders">
				<p> We interviewed multiple club builders to get real, honest insights on what the current club space was looking like. </p>
					<img src="/images/build-irl/userinterview.png" alt="User Interview" class="research-image" />

					<p>Through the interviews with builders across different community types, three insights kept surfacing:</p>

					<div class="stats-block">
						<div class="stat">
							<span class="stat__number">80%</span>
							<span class="stat__caption">were juggling 5+ disconnected tools, missing RSVPs and losing time</span>
						</div>
						<div class="stat">
							<span class="stat__number">65%</span>
							<span class="stat__caption">were burning out on unsustainable event logistics</span>
						</div>
						<div class="stat">
							<span class="stat__number">44%</span>
							<span class="stat__caption">said their members hesitate to join because they can't tell what a club is like</span>
						</div>
					</div>

					<blockquote class="pull-quote">"I spend hours on invitations and logistics. It's draining."</blockquote>

					<p class="callout">
						💡 Before touching a design, we wanted to know
						exactly <em>why</em> builders were burning out.
					</p>
				</CaseStudySubsection>
			</CaseStudySection>

			<CaseStudySection id="ideation" title="Ideation">
				<CaseStudySubsection title="Synthesizing research into patterns">
					<p>
						We turned interviews into affinity maps, personas, and insight statements — looking for the patterns that
						would give the design something concrete to solve for.
					</p>
					<img src="/images/build-irl/affinitymap.png" alt="Affinity Map" class="research-image" />
					<p class="image-caption" style="font-style: italic; color: #A8A8A8; font-size: 14px; text-align: center; margin-top: 12px;">
						A glimpse into some of our affinity mapping sessions. We grouped data and research insights into clusters, then clusters into themes we
						could actually design around.
					</p>
				</CaseStudySubsection>
				<CaseStudySubsection title="Four archetypes we kept meeting">
					<p>
						Four archetypes emerged from the clusters: two on the builder side, two on the joiner side. The Inclusive
						Builder wants a warm, welcoming club. The Broad Builder is scaling a bigger audience. The Future Builder
						might start their own club someday. The Pure Joiner just wants to show up. Each came with different needs,
						and the design had to serve all four without splintering into four different products.
					</p>
					<img src="/images/build-irl/archetypes.png" alt="Archetypes" class="research-image" />
				</CaseStudySubsection>
				<CaseStudySubsection title="From rough concepts to refined flows">
					<p>
						We sketched, mapped user flows, and built lo-fi to mid-fi prototypes. Not pictured: the stakeholder
						meetings, the pivots, and the days everything on the wall got rearranged!
					</p>
					<video src="/images/build-irl/summary.mp4" autoplay loop muted playsinline class="research-image"></video>
				</CaseStudySubsection>
			</CaseStudySection>

			<CaseStudySection id="solution" title="Solution">
				<CaseStudySubsection title="Club Joiner Flow">
					<p>
						Research showed joiners hesitate when they can't see what a club is really like. The joiner flow surfaces
						vibe, interests, and personality upfront — so the decision to join isn't a blind leap.
					</p>
					<video src="/images/build-irl/video-1.mp4" autoplay loop muted playsinline class="mockup-video"></video>
				</CaseStudySubsection>
				<CaseStudySubsection title="Club Builder Flow">
					<p>
						The builder flow offers three entry points so builders can meet the product where they are: build from
						scratch if they have a clear vision, use AI for a jumpstart, or import from Instagram to keep existing
						branding intact.
					</p>
					<div class="mockup-video-row">
					<video src="/images/build-irl/video-2.mp4" autoplay loop muted playsinline class="mockup-video"></video>
					<video src="/images/build-irl/video-3.mp4" autoplay loop muted playsinline class="mockup-video"></video>
					<video src="/images/build-irl/video-4.mp4" autoplay loop muted playsinline class="mockup-video"></video>
					</div>
					<p class="image-caption" style="font-style: italic; color: #A8A8A8; font-size: 14px; text-align: center; margin-top: 12px;">
						💡 These walkthroughs show the "Create from scratch" path, "Generate from AI" path, and the "Import from Instagram" path.
					</p>
				</CaseStudySubsection>
			</CaseStudySection>

			<CaseStudySection id="reflection" title="Reflection">
				<CaseStudySubsection title="Lessons Learned">
					<p><strong>Adaptability was the actual job.</strong> The project pivoted more times than I can count. Being ready to redesign a flow overnight wasn't a nice-to-have — it was the work.</p>
					<p><strong>Align early, align often.</strong> The design decisions that didn't get pushed back on were the ones I'd already walked stakeholders through days before.</p>
					<p><strong>Every design decision should point back to research.</strong> When I could tie a choice to a specific quote or affinity cluster, arguments about the design ended fast.</p>
				</CaseStudySubsection>
				<CaseStudySubsection title="What I'd Explore Further">
					<p>🎉 <strong>Onboarding completion rate</strong> — how many builders finish the setup flow after they start?</p>
					<p>🚦 <strong>Drop-off points inside the creation flow</strong> — where does momentum die?</p>
					<p>⏱️ <strong>Time-to-first-club</strong> — from install to a published club page, how long does it actually take?</p>
				</CaseStudySubsection>
			</CaseStudySection>

			<div class="end-cta">
				<h2 class="end-cta__heading">Want to learn more?</h2>
				<p class="end-cta__text">
					I'd love to walk you through the process, the pivots, and the parts that didn't make it into this write-up.
				</p>
			</div>
</CaseStudyLayout>

<style>
	.stats-block {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: row;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 32px;
		margin-top: 32px;
	}

	.stat {
		flex: 1;
		min-width: 180px;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		text-align: center;
	}

	.stat__number {
		font-family: 'Instrument Serif', serif;
		font-size: 60px;
		font-weight: 400;
		line-height: 1;
		color: #4483F0;
	}

	.stat__caption {
		margin-top: 12px;
		font-family: 'Work Sans', sans-serif;
		font-size: 16px;
		font-weight: 400;
		line-height: 1.4;
		color: #000;
	}

	.pull-quote {
		margin: 60px 0;
		padding: 0;
		border: none;
		font-family: 'Instrument Serif', serif;
		font-size: 32px;
		font-style: italic;
		font-weight: 400;
		line-height: 1.3;
		text-align: center;
		color: #000;
	}

	.callout {
		margin: 0;
		font-family: 'Work Sans', sans-serif;
		font-size: 18px;
		font-style: italic;
		font-weight: 400;
		line-height: 1.5;
		text-align: center;
		color: #a8a8a8;
	}

	:global(.subsection-body p + p) {
		margin-top: 1.5em;
	}

	.hero-videos {
		display: flex;
		gap: 16px;
		justify-content: center;
		align-items: center;
		margin: 24px auto 0;
		max-width: 700px;
	}

	.hero-video-half {
		flex: 1;
		max-width: 300px;
		border-radius: 20px;
		display: block;
	}
	.research-image {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    margin: 32px auto 32px;
    border-radius: 8px;
}
.mockup-video {
    display: block;
    max-height: 500px;
    width: auto;
    margin: 24px auto;
    border-radius: 12px;
}

.mockup-video-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 16px;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin: 24px auto;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
}

.mockup-video-row .mockup-video {
    max-height: 380px;
}

	@media (max-width: 768px) {
		.stats-block {
			flex-direction: column;
			gap: 24px;
		}

		.stat {
			min-width: 0;
		}

		.stat__number {
			font-size: 40px;
		}

		.stat__caption {
			font-size: 15px;
		}

		.pull-quote {
			margin: 40px 0;
			font-size: 24px;
		}

		.callout {
			font-size: 16px;
		}

		.hero-videos {
			flex-direction: column;
			max-width: 100%;
		}

		.hero-video-half {
			max-width: 100%;
			width: 100%;
		}

		.mockup-video-row {
			flex-direction: column;
			align-items: center;
		}

		.mockup-video-row .mockup-video,
		.mockup-video {
			max-height: 280px;
			width: 100%;
			max-width: 100%;
		}

		.research-image {
			max-width: 100%;
		}
	}
</style>
